 "section_summary": "This section completes Ambassador Joseph C. Grew’s despatch assessing Japan’s trade, gold reserves and vulnerability to economic sanctions. Grew compares Japanese trade returns with British and Chungking Embassy analyses and concludes that sanctions could cause severe disruption, but the available statistics do not prove they would cause Japan’s collapse. Two newspaper clippings and three translated Japanese articles follow, reporting trade figures and debating British and American economic pressure.",
