   "about": "Discusses possible British and American sanctions against Japan through the example of sanctions on Italy.",
   "summary": "The article portrays British and American aid to China as interference and sets out possible measures against Japanese trade, finance and shipping. It compares these measures with League of Nations sanctions on Italy, arguing that restrictions strengthened Italian resolve while straining its industry. It concedes that closing export markets would hurt Japan severely, but questions whether Britain and the United States would carry out comprehensive restrictions. The article continues beyond page 451.",
